# SRG-APP-000069-AU-000420  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must retain the Standard Mandatory DoW Notice and
# Consent Banner on the screen until users acknowledge the usage conditions
# and take explicit actions to log on for further access.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000069-AU-000420
group:           V-221906
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000050
control_rev5:    AC-8

contribution:    Content set in web.conf login_content stays on the Splunk Web login page
                 for as long as the page is displayed and is cleared only when the user
                 takes the explicit action of submitting credentials, so the application
                 can hold the notice on screen until the user acts to log on; Splunk Web
                 offers no separate acknowledgment control or consent checkbox that must be
                 cleared before the credential fields become usable.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] login_content non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] login_content matches You are accessing a U\.S\. Government \(USG\) Information System \(IS\)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] login_content https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/developing-views-and-apps-for-splunk-web/9.0/customize-splunk-web/customize-the-login-page
# --- end vendor verification

external:        An explicit acknowledgment step - a dialog the user must dismiss, or a
                 checkbox that must be selected before logon proceeds - is not a Splunk
                 Enterprise setting. Where the organization requires a click-through
                 acknowledgment, it is carried by a single sign-on portal or reverse proxy
                 placed ahead of Splunk Web, or by the script-based dialog in the product
                 STIG fix text, which this release's HTML sanitization of login_content may
                 remove.
external:        As with the banner display requirement, the product STIG scopes this to
                 the instance used as a search head, and access paths that bypass the
                 Splunk Web login page are covered by their own banners.
external:        Retaining the banner on screen until the user acknowledges it, which
                 Splunk Web has no setting for: login_content places the text on the login
                 page and the page proceeds on submission, so the acknowledgement half of
                 the requirement is carried outside the application.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:233-237 (login_content = <string>, no
                 default, HTML sanitized by removing potentially dangerous tags and
                 attributes); SRG-APP-000069-AU-000420 check and fix text; product STIG
                 SPLK-CL-000080 fix text for the banner wording.
finding:         Splunk Web does not retain the Standard Mandatory Notice and Consent
                 Banner until the user acts to log on, because web.conf [settings]
                 login_content carries no banner text for the login page to hold; this is
                 assessed at the application layer alone, and an explicit acknowledgment
                 control, for which Splunk Enterprise has no setting, is recorded as an
                 external dependency carried by a single sign-on portal or reverse proxy
                 ahead of Splunk Web.
